From: ILFforever <hammymukura@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 15:41:34 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] X-H2 controls: Q, PLAY, DRIVE, VIEW, Fn1 and Fn2 from the
 5.20 key readers

- Q: a rung on the ADC 6 ladder, 3103..3776 (reader 0x13fe8b8, scanner row 27).
- PLAY, DRIVE/delete, VIEW MODE: a new ADC 5 ladder (readers 0x13feac0,
  0x13fea2c, 0x13fe998; rows 20-22), 3103..3776 / 2637..3102 / 2117..2344.
- Fn1 / Fn2: GPIO 0.4 / 0.15, active low (scanner rows 4 and 5, FUNCTION and
  FUNCTION2).

The band words come from the factory key-band table read through 0x148f2e8,
checked against the existing MENU/OK and DISP/BACK rungs. Verified on the 5.20
board under the merged emulator: Q opens the Quick Menu and PLAY opens
playback. Written against the xh2-blanny branch's ADC 6 ladder.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
